{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Honor.</b> It is a noun and it always has a kamatz, except when it is in construct state, as in וְאֶת־יְקַר תִּפְאֶרֶת גְּדֻלָּתוֹ. And if it is an adjective, the yod takes a kamatz gadol, and when it is in construct state it merges with the governed noun. יְקַר רוּחַ is not understanding, and the meaning distinguishes between them."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:05.495736438Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}